(5) WHEN THE LAW FAILS -- is it always q0 > 14?
    (the classical sieve lemma proves q divides no speed => 1/q lonely
     ONLY for q <= 14, since ||v/q|| >= 1/q needs 1/q >= 1/14)
    q0 <= 14:  454 families, law fails   0 (0.0%)
    q0 >  14:   46 families, law fails  16 (34.8%)

    => if the law NEVER fails for q0 <= 14, that is the classical lemma
       confirmed; the open content is exactly the q0 > 14 regime.

